    "hypothesis": "New checkout tasks are crash-looping on startup due to an out-of-memory error: each replacement task logs 'WARN memory pressure rising' then attempts to allocate a 900MiB cache and dies with MemoryError/OOM (task <PHONE_3> shows explicit Python MemoryError traceback). ECS keeps launching replacement tasks (<PHONE_4>, <PHONE_5>, <PHONE_7>, <PHONE_8>) roughly every 30-80s, each repeating the same fatal pattern, which explains tasks_pending=2 and deployments_in_flight=2 while tasks_running stays pinned at desired count (the two original long-lived tasks <PHONE_1>/<PHONE_2> are unaffected and keep heartbeating). Likely cause: a startup cache/allocation path requesting ~900MiB exceeds the container's memory limit or available headroom, possibly triggered by increased load, a data-size change, or a leak/regression in the cache-warming code — not a code deploy (RECENT DEPLOYS is empty), so more likely a data-driven or environmental trigger (e.g., larger dataset/config causing the cache alloc to grow, or reduced available memory from another process).",
